e opponent has called my aggressive bets on the flop and turn, staying in despite the spade-heavy board. This calling pattern strongly suggests they either have a spade (flush) or are committed with a strong hand. Betting here would be throwing chips away. Checking is the prudent play - it costs nothing, allows me to see showdown if opponent also checks, and minimizes losses if they bet (indicating strength). I can fold to any bet, preserving my chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
